# Video mode, the timeline editor (docs/design/future/video-nle.md): import a clip, make a 9:16 timeline, place, cut,
# ripple delete, unlink, reframe, play and export; each step captured for review. Needs a display and ffmpeg
# (just qa-editor Tests/QA/video.qa); not in CI. It runs on the Demo project and leaves its Assets/Video and Exports
# folders as it found them (none). The fixture is build/make-video-fixture.sh's 12 s test pattern (a 440 Hz tone silent
# from 4 to 6 s, with a sidecar). `wait N` counts frames; the long steps wait on conditions: `wait-for video-jobs` (no
# probe, import or export left) and `wait-for video-position`. Review the PNGs in artifacts/qa-editor.
wait-for project 300
video reset
mode video
wait 20
capture video-01-empty
video import Tests/QA/Fixtures/video/sample.mp4
wait-for video-jobs 60
video timeline Vertical QA Edit
wait-for video-jobs 60
wait 30
capture video-02-new-timeline
video source Assets/Video/Media/sample.mp4
wait-for video-jobs 60
wait 30
capture video-03-source
command video.overwrite
wait 30
capture video-04-placed
# Cut 3-6 s out of the clip (and its sound) and close the gap.
video seek 3
command video.add_edit_all
video seek 6
command video.add_edit_all
video select V1 4.5
command video.ripple_delete
wait 30
capture video-05-ripple
# The picture fills the 9:16 frame; then fit it at 100 %, letterboxed.
video select V1 1
video fit 0 100
wait 30
capture video-06-fit
command video.link
wait 10
video select A1 1
wait 10
capture video-07-unlinked
command edit.undo
video seek 0
command video.play
wait-for video-position 2 30
capture video-08-playing
command video.play
video export vertical-30
wait 10
capture video-09-export-dialog
accept
wait-for video-jobs 300
wait 20
capture video-10-exported
accept
mode game
video reset
